# Its id leads with aspect-: a State of the same name (Raging, Mindful, God Ki) has the bare one.
id: aspect-scaling
name: Scaling
polarity: positive
levels: true
max: 4
# [Solo]: its levels are not added between Transformations used together - the highest of them.
solo: true
# number: its script is the whole of it. moment: entering, leaving, the start of a turn (stages 4-5).
# rule: how a Transformation is entered, left or Mastered - asked by transformations.mjs aspectLevel.
group: rule
# The rule in short, for its hovers; its own words below (the page the user gave, 2026-11-20).
summary: >
  A Higher Scale for each Tier of Power above its original ToP Requirement (up to its level), chosen as you enter; each: Attribute Bonuses (but SC/IN/PE) +1(T), Stress Test Requirement +2, ToP Requirement +1.
text: >
  Scaling [Solo, LV~4]: This Transformation’s power grows with you.
  –Effect: For each Tier of Power you exceed the original (before any modifications) Tier of Power Requirement of this Transformation, it gains a Higher Scale. A Transformation can possess a number of Higher Scales up to their level of the Scaling Aspect.

  When attempting to enter a Transformation, you may select how many Higher Scales (if any) the Transformation has applied. While in the Transformation, you can spend 1 Action to make a Stress Test for this Transformation with a different number of Higher Scales (if any) applied. If you succeed, the number of Higher Scales applied to this Transformation changes to the different amount you selected.

  For each Higher Scale, increase the Attribute Modifier Bonuses (except SC/IN/PE) of the Transformation by 1(T), the Stress Test Requirement by 2, and the Tier of Power Requirement by 1.

---

# Nothing it does by itself yet: the Transformation Maneuver and Mastery read it.
